    "originalInstructions": "1. Mix one large teacupful of cracker crumbs, one quart of milk, one spoonful of flour, a pinch of salt, the yolks of three eggs, one whole egg and half a cupful of sugar\n2. Flavor with vanilla, adding a little pinch of salt\n3. Bake in a moderate oven\n4. When done, spread over the top, while hot, a pint of well-sugared raspberries\n5. Beat the whites of the three eggs very stiff, with two tablespoonfuls of sugar, a little lemon extract, or whatever one prefers\n6. Spread this over the berries and bake a light brown\n7. Serve with fruit sauce made of raspberries",
